{
  "dom_id": "step-q172158",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{2}{5}÷8=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $8$ is $\\frac{1}{8}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\,÷\\,8=\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{2\\times 1}{5\\times 8}=\\frac{2}{40}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{40}=\\frac{2÷2}{40÷2}=\\frac{1}{20}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
